.el .ds Aq '
.TH bbcli 1  "bbcli " 
.SH NAME
bbcli \- BarterBackup CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbbcli\fR [\fB\-\-local\-addr\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
BarterBackup CLI
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-local\-addr\fR \fI<LOCAL_ADDR>\fR
local_addr is the local daemon endpoint
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBBBCLI_LOCAL_ADDR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<DATA_DIR>\fR
data_dir is the base directory for daemon state and local CLI keys
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBBBCLI_DATA_DIR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bbcli\-state(1)
Print daemon state
.TP
bbcli\-init(1)
Initialize daemon storage with the main password
.TP
bbcli\-unlock(1)
Send the main password to the daemon unlock path
.TP
bbcli\-stop(1)
Ask the daemon to shut down gracefully
.TP
bbcli\-peer(1)
Manage known peers
.TP
bbcli\-file(1)
Manage files in the latest encrypted content blob
.TP
bbcli\-contract(1)
Inspect and drive contracts with peers
.TP
bbcli\-recovery(1)
Run recovery and resolve divergent revisions
.TP
bbcli\-config(1)
Read or update daemon configuration
.TP
bbcli\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
